---
// Sample report text comes from `horsy audit --demo` (synthetic sessions). Numbers are verbatim;
// the Share line and some --plan max rows are omitted. Checked against `--demo --json` by a script outside the repo.
---
<section class="audit" id="audit" aria-labelledby="audit-h">
  <div class="wrap audit-grid">
    <div class="audit-copy">
      <h2 id="audit-h">Run it once. See where the money goes.</h2>
      <p class="lede">The audit reads your local Claude Code transcripts, prices them at API list rates, and flags subagent tasks that ran on a bigger model than they needed. It is an estimate, and nothing leaves your machine.</p>
      <div class="acmd">
        <code>npx @horsy/cli audit</code>
        <p>Not on npm yet. Until release, run it from the repo:</p>
        <div class="repo-row on-paper pillbox"><code class="repo" id="audit-repo">git clone https://github.com/paoloxia/horsy &amp;&amp; ./horsy/packages/plugin/bin/horsy audit</code><button type="button" class="copybtn on-paper" data-copy="#audit-repo">copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tote" aria-label="Headline figures from the sample report below">
        <p class="tote-h">From the sample report</p>
        <p><b>$4.75</b><span>API-equivalent spend over 30 days</span></p>
        <p><b>14</b><span>simple subagent tasks that ran on Opus</span></p>
        <p class="hot"><b>$1.12</b><span>could cost less on Sonnet · Haiku unproven</span></p>
      </div>
      <p class="anext">Step two is the plugin in shadow mode: it shows what it would have routed, and what that would have saved.</p>
      <a class="textlink dk" href="#race">How the plugin works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </div>

    <div class="audit-sheet-col">
      <figure class="sheet" aria-label="Sample audit report on synthetic demo sessions">
        <figcaption class="sheet-bar"><span>horsy audit --demo</span><em>Sample report on synthetic demo sessions</em></figcaption>
        <div class="sheet-body">
          <p class="s-meta">12 sessions · 3 projects · 2026-09-16 → 2026-10-16 · 4 lines skipped<br/>Demo data (synthetic)</p>
          <p class="s-note">Estimate: your local Claude Code transcripts priced at API list rates. Nothing leaves this machine.</p>

          <h3 class="s-h"><span>SPEND</span> ~$4.75 API-equivalent · 2.8M tokens</h3>
          <p class="s-note">Paying per token? These are your dollars. On Max/Pro you pay a flat fee: rerun with --plan max to see tokens.</p>
          <dl class="s-rows">
            <dt>Models</dt><dd><span class="nw">opus-5-5 $4.17 (88%)</span> · <span class="nw">sonnet-5-5 $0.56 (12%)</span> · <span class="nw">haiku-5-5 $0.02 (&lt;1%)</span></dd>
            <dt>Subagents</dt><dd>65% of spend ($3.10)</dd>
            <dt>Main sessions</dt><dd><span class="nw">35% of spend ($1.65): opus-5-5 $1.60 (97%)</span> · <span class="nw">sonnet-5-5 $0.05 (3%)</span></dd>
            <dt>Cache</dt><dd>73% of input came from cache (higher is better)</dd>
            <dt>Projects</dt><dd><span class="nw">project-1 $2.44 (51%)</span> · <span class="nw">project-2 $1.33 (28%)</span> · <span class="nw">project-3 $0.98 (21%)</span></dd>
            <dt>Busiest days</dt><dd><span class="nw">2026-10-04 534k tok ($1.01)</span> · <span class="nw">2026-10-01 401k tok ($0.85)</span> · <span class="nw">2026-10-12 361k tok ($0.52)</span></dd>
          </dl>

          <h3 class="s-h"><span>DELEGATED TASKS</span></h3>
          <table class="s-tab">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">class (guessed)</th><th scope="col">model</th><th scope="col" class="n">tasks</th><th scope="col" class="n">cost</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>explain</td><td>opus-5-5</td><td class="n">5</td><td class="n">$0.80</td></tr>
              <tr><td>search</td><td>opus-5-5</td><td class="n">5</td><td class="n">$0.78</td></tr>
              <tr><td>read</td><td>opus-5-5</td><td class="n">3</td><td class="n">$0.49</td></tr>
              <tr><td>implement</td><td>sonnet-5-5</td><td class="n">3</td><td class="n">$0.25</td></tr>
              <tr><td>implement</td><td>opus-5-5</td><td class="n">1</td><td class="n">$0.19</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p class="s-note">+7 more (use --json for all)</p>
          <p class="s-note">class is guessed from the task description; -wide = touches many files</p>

          <h3 class="s-h"><span>COULD COST LESS</span></h3>
          <p class="s-line">~$1.12 on 14 simple subagent tasks that ran on Opus, if rerun on Sonnet (Haiku: unproven in your repo, up to ~$2.18); assumes equal quality</p>
          <p class="s-line">+ $0.05 rework: 1 task failed or was dispatched more than once</p>
          <p class="s-line">+ $0.24 context: 1 session started with &gt; 50k tokens (cache writes above 50k)</p>

          <h3 class="s-h"><span>TOP THINGS TO CHANGE</span> (savings are estimates, scaled to 30 days)</h3>
          <ol class="s-top">
            <li><b>Send search/read/explain/rename subagents to Sonnet: 14 tasks ran on Opus.</b>
              <span>→ Pass <code>model: "sonnet"</code> (or set <code>model: sonnet</code> in the agent's definition) for search/read/explain subagents. Haiku: unproven in your repo. The Horsy plugin can do this per task, in shadow mode first.</span>
              <i>(est. saving ~$1.12/month)</i></li>
            <li><b>1 session started with &gt; 50k tokens of context.</b>
              <span>→ Trim CLAUDE.md, unused MCP servers and skills loaded at startup.</span>
              <i>(est. saving ~$0.24/month)</i></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="s-note">Only 2 findings stood out.</p>

          <h3 class="s-h"><span>TIPS</span></h3>
          <p class="s-line">- Your longest session re-reads ~81k tokens of context every turn</p>
          <p class="s-line">→ /clear between unrelated tasks, /compact when switching topic.</p>

          <p class="s-note">Prices: Anthropic API list prices as of 2026-10-19</p>
        </div>
      </figure>

      <div class="planmax">
        <p><b>On a Max or Pro plan?</b> Run with <code>--plan max</code>. The report leads with tokens, not dollars:</p>
        <code class="pm">SPEND  2.8M tokens (≈ $4.75 at API list prices)<br/>Busiest 5-hour windows (UTC, approximate: this machine only; your real reset may differ)<br/>2026-10-04 15:00 +5h 534k tok</code>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
